  "user_scenario": "You are Darrell Kucera, seventy-one, who farms irrigated corn and soybeans outside Ord, Nebraska, and keeps a good share of the family's savings in the association's Class H preferred stock. It is Friday morning, July 24, 2026, and you are calling from the kitchen table with your reading glasses on. You have some cash sitting idle and you want to buy as much Class H preferred stock as the rules allow right now, paid straight out of your checking account the association already has on file for your preferred stock. You do not know how much that comes to and you want the agent to work it out from your records; you are not interested in buying less than the most you are allowed. The purchase is yours to authorize, so when the agent hands it to you, you place it yourself for exactly the amount the agent tells you.\n\nWhen asked who you are, you give your phone number, 7854652416. To verify you, you read your member number, CPF-5390127, off last year's equity statement, and if one more detail is needed the last four of your Social Security number are 9137. Only if asked for your email do you give darrell.kucera@outlook.com, and only if asked when you became a member, November 4, 2003, which is 2003-11-04. If the agent asks which account, it is your checking ending 5418, the one your preferred stock dividends and payouts already go to.\n\nYou do not bring up anything else about your preferred stock. Only if the agent asks whether you bought any preferred stock recently do you say yes, you mailed a check for two hundred ninety thousand dollars in May after you sold some ground. If the agent explains that something on your preferred stock has to be corrected, cancelled, refunded or reversed first, you say that is fine with you, go ahead, and you wait; if the agent tells you an amount that was refunded to your checking or taken back, you say all right, you trust the books. When the agent tells you the most you can buy, you do not argue or ask for a different number, and once the purchase is handed to you, you place it for that amount and read back the purchase reference if asked. When the agent confirms the purchase went through, you thank them and hang up.",
